DESCRIPTION:Get your tickets here\nOr contact the MAC box office: 812-855-7
 433\n\n  \nWhat is it about Beethoven’s 9th Symphony that sets it apart? Ma
 ybe it’s the innovative musical structure. Maybe it’s the way Beethoven ble
 nds themes of chaos\, redemption\, grace\, and struggle so effortlessly. Or
  it could be that this piece culminates\, as John Henken of the LA Philharm
 onic writes\, “expressing our highest aspirations with music of life-affirm
 ing exaltation.” \nFor the first time in our history the BSO will perform B
 eethoven’s iconic 9th Symphony. Joined by a 100+ member community chorus on
  the stage of Indiana University’s Musical Arts Center (MAC)\, this is sure
  to be an unforgettable concert experience that will also feature a world p
 remiere piece by Daixuan Ai. Read her program notes here. \nParticipating c
 hoirs include the Bloomington Chamber Singers (Caio Lopes\, director)\, Voc
 es Novae (Sue Swaney\, director) and the choir of the Unitarian Universalis
 t Church (Sue Swaney\, director)\, as well as individuals from many other l
 ocal choirs. The choirs are all coming together under the direction of Dr. 
 Betsy Burleigh. \nVocal soloists (click here for bios):Soprano: Nathalie Fr
 iederichAlto: Esther JoTenor: Suro KimBass: Stephen Stavnicky \nAdults: $25
 \, Students: $12\, Children under 18: Free\nSaturday May 16\, 2026\, at the
  IU Musical Arts Center\n6:15pm pre-concert talk with Daixuan Ai and Ryo Ha
 segawa\n7:00pm concert \nGet your tickets here\nOr contact the MAC box offi
 ce:\n812-855-7433\n101 North Eagleson Avenue\nBloomington\, IN 47405\nMonda
 y–Friday | 11:30 a.m.–5:30 p.m.
